<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-197] parquet-cascading and the mapred API does not create metadata file</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-197</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Repro: run a scalding job that writes parquet files to a folder. no _metadata and _common_metadata file is created&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Impact: potential performance problem if parquet metadata is read from client side, which is the case for sparkSQL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;casue: the metatdata writing logic is in the mapreduce API but not the mapred API of parquet.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
